# Orca's game patches for Project+ v3.2 (launcher profile PPLUS32, on Super Smash Bros. Brawl NTSC-U
# revision 2), forced on in every Project+ session (Source/Core/Core/Orca/UX/GamePatches.h):
# `<address> <original> <value>`, hex. Applied only once the launcher has handed over to the game
# (the profile's frame hook is live), and only as guarded groups: a group is written while every
# one of its words is still the original, so nothing ever lands in Project+'s own codes or in
# another module that later occupies the memory. Never a `*` line: Project+ owns the game's data
# (the one data group below sets a default once, then leaves the words to the game).
# This file is hashed into the lobby key.
#
# Groups: the boot's save prompt skipped; the main menu's Play Online, the game's own ONLINE page
# with no connection and every way on from it to the local Versus character select, and B from
# there back to the page it came from (ORCA.md "Online menu"; Orca's texture pack relabels With
# Anyone CASUAL / RANKED, UX/MenuText.h drops "(Discontinued)"); the rules' items off by default;
# Options > Sound's balance held in the middle.

# muBootNandTask (Brawl's sora_menu_boot, loaded at 0x811A6000 on the boot scene; process
# 0x811A6300, state at +0x78), which Project+ loads unchanged at the same address (the six original
# words checked in Project+'s RAM on the save prompt, 2026-10-02). With no save in the session NAND
# (always so with Orca.app), state 5 opens Project+'s "Create save file for Project+?" and, on Yes,
# spends about 13 s writing a 14.6 MB Brawl save to the NAND before character select. In its place,
# as RSBE01.patches does for Brawl: the game's own "continue without saving" (clear the save flags,
# +0x48 &= 0xE0, and go to state 55, the end of the boot check). No dialog, no save written;
# Project+ goes on to character select by itself. A session that seeds a save never reaches state 5.
811A6430 80030068 88030048    # lbz   r0, 0x48(r3)
811A6434 83E3005C 54000634    # rlwinm r0, r0, 0, 24, 26
811A6438 2C000000 98030048    # stb   r0, 0x48(r3)
811A643C 4182001C 38000037    # li    r0, 55
811A6440 7C030378 90030078    # stw   r0, 0x78(r3)
811A6444 4AF193ED 48001204    # b     0x811A7648 (the process's end)

# Boot to the main menu, not the character select (booting should land on the
# home menu, as Brawl's does). Project+'s codeset boots straight to its VERSUS character select:
# "Boot Directly to CSS v5.4" (Source/Project+/BootToCSS.asm on the SD card, in NETBOOST.GCT, which
# the codeset's expansion loader reads to 0x80550010) hooks sqBoot::setNext at 0x806DD5F8 and,
# unless a pad holds L/R (Training), Start (the title) or Z (Replays) right then, starts sqVsMelee
# in place of the game's sqPrizeCheck. The hook's branch and the nop after it are the code
# handler's, written again every frame; the code they reach is NETBOOST.GCT's own words, which
# nothing writes after the load. Its "no special input" case takes the Start case's path instead:
# sqPrizeCheck with 0x14, which goes on to the title and the main menu as vanilla Brawl does (the
# title is skipped below, the prizes by the codeset's own Netplay.asm).
80559C20 41A0FF84 41A0FF84    # blt   the pad loop (guard)
80559C24 38951B54 38951C94    # addi  r4, r21, 0x1B54 ("sqVsMelee") -> 0x1C94 ("sqPrizeCheck")
80559C28 38A00000 38A00014    # li    r5, 0 -> 0x14 (as the Start case)
80559C2C 48000038 48000038    # b     the hook's end (guard)

# scTitle (sora_scene, which Project+ keeps), skipped as RSBE01.patches skips it for Brawl: the
# opening movie and the "press Start" logo both become state 16, the title's exit with result 0,
# which sqTitle takes to the main menu.
806CA1F8 38000003 38000010    # li r0, 3 -> 16 (the opening movie)
806CA204 3800000C 38000010    # li r0, 12 -> 16 (the "press Start" logo)

# The main menu's Play Online (RSBE01.patches describes these groups for Brawl): the game's own
# ONLINE page with no connection, and every way on from it to the local Versus character select.
# Project+ replaces sora_menu_main with its own build of the module (/Project+/pf/module), loaded at
# 0x81164C00, whose code sits at the same offsets as Brawl's: every address below is Brawl's
# + 0x1480 (each original word read in Project+'s RAM on its main menu, 2026-10-02). Project+'s
# button already says PLAY ONLINE and its pages ONLINE; without these groups A on it showed
# "There is no save data. Unable to access Wiimmfi." (the connection window's save check).
#
# muProcTop's update: A on Play Online enters its page like every other button, never creating the
# connection window. Two copies of the press check.
81179ED8 A01D0042 A01D0042    # lhz    r0, 0x42(r29) (the cursor; guard)
81179EDC 28000002 28000002    # cmplwi r0, 2 (guard)
81179EE0 4082007C 4800007C    # bne +0x7C -> b +0x7C

8117A0B0 A01D0042 A01D0042    # lhz    r0, 0x42(r29) (guard)
8117A0B4 28000002 28000002    # cmplwi r0, 2 (guard)
8117A0B8 4082007C 4800007C    # bne +0x7C -> b +0x7C

